  "has_issues": true,
  "issues": [
    "EBITDA is said to add back depreciation and amortization, yet the same definition also claims to exclude 'non-cash items'—D&A are non-cash, so both statements cannot simultaneously be true as written.",
    "Restructuring costs are listed among 'exclusions' but also described as 'capped at 15% of EBITDA'—caps are typically applied to add-backs, implying conflicting treatment (excluded vs added back).",
    "Risk section says the modified leverage ratio includes multiple calculation periods, while the Key Covenants define it solely using trailing twelve months, creating an inconsistency about the measurement window."
